Subject: [PATCH 03059/11362] [outer-loop] FINDING: the E3+v3 cascade loses to
 bare BFS in bounded compute (esp. action efficiency = the scoring metric)

Second sim (post value_weight->0 revert): E3 cascade+v3 head solves 3/25 (19 timeouts, 83-101s/game);
bare BFS solves 4/25 (24/25 completed, 1-56s). Decisive on action efficiency (the score metric): lp85
BFS 21 actions vs cascade 7792 actions -> cascade scores ~0 even when it solves. Root cause: the v3 head
is LOADED + its expensive features computed per-node for tiebreaking even at value_weight=0 (zero benefit)
+ the E3 induction tier overhead. RECOMMEND: (1) gate the v3-head load on value_weight>0 (None at 0), (2)
strongly consider submitting the bare-BFS explorer (8/32 baseline) not the cascade -- the cascade's only
justification (the LLM tier) was 0/6 value-added and it destroys action efficiency.

